===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|Lucy}}, from {{der|en|fro|Lucie}} (notably after the Christian martyr {{w|Saint Lucy|Lucia of Syracuse}}), from {{der|en|la|Lucia}} (feminine of {{m|la|Lucius}}, a Roman [[praenomen]]), from {{m|la|lux||light}}.

The name of the {{taxfmt|Australopithecus|genus}} skeleton came from the [[Beatles]] song "{{w|Lucy in the Sky with Diamonds}}", which was being played repeatedly at the dig site camp at the time of the discovery. The slang term for LSD also derives from the song name, which many believe is essentially a reference to the drug.

